/* max_array_r: intermediate level of max_array, written by hand (PipelineB, refinement step), the
   component BART refines.
   Purpose: replace max(ran(array)) by the two facts a loop establishes: the result is a value of
   the array, and no position holds a greater value. The proof that these two facts define
   max(ran(array)) is thus done once, here, away from the loop. Same level as max_array_r of the
   B Workbook, with 0..NN written in place of dom(array). */
REFINEMENT
    max_array_r

REFINES
    max_array

SEES
    ctx

OPERATIONS

    maxi <-- getMaximum(array) =
    PRE
        array : (0..NN) --> INT
    THEN
        maxi :( maxi : ran(array) &
                !index.(index : 0..NN => array(index) <= maxi) )
    END

END
